content.p:
Approves the summary for policymakers of the thematic assessment of the sustainable use of wild species,
IPBES/9/14/Add.1. and accepts the chapters of the assessment, including their executive summaries;
IPBES/9/INF/1/Rev.1.

Also approves the summary for policymakers of the methodological assessment of the diverse values and valuation of nature,
IPBES/9/14/Add.2. and accepts the chapters of the assessment, including their executive summaries;
IPBES/9/INF/2/Rev.1.

Welcomes the report on progress set out in the note by the secretariat on engagement with the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change
IPBES/9/9. and takes note of the compilation of suggestions for thematic or methodological issues related to biodiversity and climate change that would benefit from collaboration between the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change and the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services;
IPBES/9/INF/26.

Regional online or in-person dialogues with programmers and funders on the generation of new knowledge, focused mainly on the gaps identified in the Methodological Assessment Report on the Diverse Values and Valuation of Nature
IPBES (2022): Methodological Assessment Report on the Diverse Values and Valuation of Nature of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services. P. Balvanera, U. Pascual, M. Christie, B. Baptiste, D. González-Jiménez (eds.). IPBES secretariat, Bonn, Germany. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6522522. and the Thematic Assessment Report on the Sustainable Use of Wild Species
IPBES (2022): Thematic Assessment Report on the Sustainable Use of Wild Species of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services. J.-M. Fromentin, M.R. Emery, J. Donaldson, M.-C. Danner, A. Hallosserie, D. Kieling (eds.). IPBES secretariat, Bonn, Germany. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6448567. (January/February 2023);

Collation of materials of relevance to indigenous peoples and local communities from the Thematic Assessment Report on the Sustainable Use of Wild Species
IPBES (2022): Assessment Report on the Diverse Values and Valuation of Nature of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services. P. Balvanera, U. Pascual, M. Christie, B. Baptiste, D. González-Jiménez (eds.). IPBES secretariat, Bonn, Germany. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6522522. and the Methodological Assessment Report on the Diverse Values and Valuation of Nature
IPBES (2022): Assessment Report on the Sustainable Use of Wild Species of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services. J.-M. Fromentin, M.R. Emery, J. Donaldson, M.-C. Danner, A. Hallosserie, D. Kieling (eds.). IPBES secretariat, Bonn, Germany. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6448567. and their dissemination in all six official United Nations languages, including, in collaboration with the task force on capacity-building, to national and regional platforms on biodiversity and ecosystem services and to indigenous peoples and local communities;

Based on considerations put forth at the ninth session of the Plenary, the further development of the foundations of the nature futures framework, a flexible tool to support the development of scenarios and models of desirable futures for people, nature and Mother Earth,
Though not repeated every time throughout the present document after "nature futures framework", it is understood that any mention of the framework implicitly includes this subtitle. including but not limited to alignment with the IPBES conceptual framework and the findings of the IPBES Methodological Assessment Report on the Diverse Values and Valuation of Nature.
IPBES (2022): Methodological Assessment Report on the Diverse Values and Valuation of Nature of the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services. P. Balvanera, U. Pascual, M. Christie, B. Baptiste, D. González-Jiménez (eds.). IPBES secretariat, Bonn, Germany. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6522522. An update on the nature futures framework foundations and a synthesis of catalysed work on scenario development across knowledge systems will be provided to the Plenary at its tenth session;
